ia.controls.airplane=Stick forward/back: throttle  Look: pitch and turn  Stick left/right: turn  Attack: fire  Sneak: get out
ia.controls.all=Works the same on touch, controller and keyboard. Planes: push the stick forward to raise the throttle and back to lower it (and brake on the ground); with look steering the plane pitches and turns toward where you look. Helicopters and airships: the stick flies forward, back and turns; look up to climb and down to descend. With stick-only steering (free look) you can look around freely: planes climb as you push forward and descend as you pull back, and helicopters and airships only climb or descend when you look far up or down. Airships keep their speed: push forward to speed up and back to slow down. The gyrodyne needs you to hold forward to spin the rotor up. Attack (on touch: tap while holding any item, or tap your aircraft) to fire weapons; the telescope zooms in on the first press and out on the next. Use a firework rocket to burn the rockets in the boost slot. Sneak (or the dismount button) to get out. Use an aircraft while holding an upgrade, weapon, banner or dye to install it. Sneak next to an aircraft and use it (the Open button on touch) to open its Java inventory or install fuel. Use a damaged aircraft to repair it. Sneak and hit an aircraft to open this panel, which can also kick out passengers. World settings: Settings > Behavior Packs > Immersive Aircraft > gear.
ia.controls.boost=Use a firework rocket to boost
ia.controls.gyrodyne=Hold forward to spin the rotor up  Look up/down: climb/descend  Sneak: get out
